' A `DO ... LOOP UNTIL` (post-test loop) miscompilation: a `MUT String`
' initialized from a literal and appended to inside the body was read as its
' stale *initial* value on every iteration, so only the final append survived
' ("ZX" instead of "ZXXXX"). The `MUT Integer` counter updated correctly, so the
' loop ran the right number of times — only the reference-typed binding's reads
' were stale, which points at the post-test loop's handling of a
' constant-initialized MUT local rather than at `&` itself.
IMPORT io

FUNC main AS Integer
  MUT s AS String = "Z"
  MUT n AS Integer = 0
  DO
    s = s & "X"
    n = n + 1
  LOOP UNTIL n >= 4
  io::print(s)
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
